 ],
 "literal": "Like the bright flower of the glory lily with bunched clusters, / the rooster with a dense red crest and a flock / watching for house rats in the deep darkness of midnight, / becoming the night prey for the young wildcat, / may you suffer severe distress! You indeed, / who woke us from the sweet, secure sleep with the chief of the fertile, watery town!",
 "translation": "O rooster with a dense red crest, resembling the bright flower of the clustered glory lily! You who lead a flock and watch for house rats in the deep darkness of midnight, only to become the night prey of a young wildcat—may you suffer severe distress! For you have woken me from my sweet, secure sleep with the lord of the fertile, watery town.",
 "modern": "குவிந்த கொத்துக்களைக் கொண்ட தோன்றிப்பூவின் பிரகாசமான மலரைப் போன்ற அடர்ந்த சிவந்த கொண்டையையும், தன் கூட்டத்தையும் உடைய சேவலே! நள்ளிருள் யாமத்தில் வீட்டு எலிகளைப் பார்த்துக் கொண்டிருக்கும் நீ, இளமையான காட்டுப்பூனைக்கு இரவாகிப் போய், கடுமையான துன்பத்தை அடைவாயாக! நீர்வளம் மிக்க புதுவருவாய் உடைய ஊரனாகிய என் தலைவனுடன் நான் கூடிப் பெற்ற இன்பமான துயிலைக் கலைத்து எழுப்பியவனே!",
 "explanation": "The speaker is the heroine (தலைவி), who is addressing a rooster in the Marutham (agricultural) landscape. She has spent a blissful night with her husband, the chief of the fertile town, but the rooster's crowing at dawn has woken them up and ended their sweet union. Frustrated by this interruption, she curses the rooster, wishing that it becomes prey to a young wildcat as it hunts for rats in the dark. The imagery of the rooster being hunted by a wildcat reflects the vulnerability of her own happiness, which is easily disrupted by external forces. Key words include 'இன்துயில்' (sweet sleep), 'ஊரன்' (chief of the town), and 'சேவல்' (rooster).",
